plenty of other topics though still  hovering over the nfl and one the  availability this weekend or next  weekend or the weekend after that of  chiefs quarterback patrick mahomes he  did not play on sunday night when the  chiefs lost to the packers chiefs are  now five and three on the year and owen  won without patrick mahomes mahomes had  told michelle tafoya of nbc before the  game that it was a playoff game he would  have played andy reid the coach of the  chiefs chimed in on this and he says  that basically it's going to come down  to what the doctors say  he reid said that mahomes during the  denver game was trying to get back in  after he had the dislocated kneecap so  mahomes wants a play and the chiefs like  that about him but ultimately it's what  the doctors think now here's the thing  to keep in mind at the risk of being  ultracynical but we know how this works  the doctors are paid by the team they  are hired by the team  and if the doctors want to continue to  be hired by the team and work for the  team and it is a very lucrative  assignment in the market where the  doctors are because  if you are providing medical care to the  local nfl team the average person is  going to assume that that must be a good  doctor so you use that to leverage a  bigger practice you make more money and  that's what capitalism's all about  so a key to that is retaining the  relationship with the local nfl team and  one key to retaining the relationship is  sometimes you got to tell them what they  want to hear  so it's not  it's not  laboratory settings it's not determined  in a vacuum  and sometimes the  the doctors and i'm not saying this is  what's going on here we just have to  recognize the bias sometimes the doctors  are listening for those clues  regarding  what they think  the patient or the person footing the  bill wants to hear and in a case like  this when the patient wants to play  you know you almost have to be careful  you don't push back too hard if you're  the doctors because the team may  ultimately say well  if the guy can play then just let him  play we're willing to take some risk if  he's willing to take some risk but  that's ultimately the decision the  chiefs have to make if they do want to  nudge the doctors or not nudge the  doctors if they just want to be ultra  safe maybe what they do in a case like  this is they nudge the doctors towards  saying he can't play so then patrick  mahomes won't get mad at the team won't  get mad at the coach for not letting him  play so you know the pressure can go  both ways  and in the old days the pressure was  always along the lines of pushing the  player  and the team to get the guy on the field  because that's what the coach wanted  now in a case like this who knows maybe  the chiefs are trying to tap the brakes  a little bit on getting mahomes back on  the field because they understand the  risk that they would be taking by  putting their most important player on  the field prematurely and potentially  getting him injured  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

